; SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
; superposition.source.vla - Superposition, a lattice of 512 by 512 sites at rate zero
; (CART.12): the engine's large board, a mine-clearing game whose every square is safe
; and dangerous at once until it is observed. The pass expands this file into
; superposition.vla beside it, the rows the engine loads (docs/SPEC.md section 7.8): edit
; this one, then expand it again with
;   cargo run --release --example expand
;
; How to play. The Field is a lattice of 262,144 sites, each in superposition, safe and
; decayed at once, until you look. Move with the arrows, Page Up and Page Down, Home and
; End, and the mouse; then:
;   observe (Space, or a click): the site collapses. A decayed site is counted, and the
;     experiment goes on; a safe one shows its reading, the decays among its eight
;     neighbors, and a reading of nothing opens every site around it, a ring a frame.
;     The first observation of a world is never a decay.
;   box (B, or the right button): seal a site you believe has decayed, or open the box.
;     A box beside a reading of nothing opens, since nothing has decayed beside nothing.
;   collapse (C, or the middle button): a reading whose boxes equal it observes every
;     site around it; a wrong box observes a decay.
;   branch (N): another world, its lattice dealt again from its number.
; The Observer sheet keeps the experiment's counts: the sites observed, the boxes, the
; decays observed and the sites still in superposition. Constants!B1 holds the decay
; probability, 0.15, which anyone may edit; at 0.09 one opening spans the lattice.
; Clock!B3 is the seed: everyone who types the same seed observes the same worlds.
;
; The words are quantum mechanics', and the game is a mine-clearing game's: a mine is a
; decay, a flag a box, a chord a collapse, a new game a branch to another world.
;
; How it settles. The cartridge says (settle 4096): after an act the engine steps the
; lattice again, with no act, until a frame changes nothing (docs/SPEC.md section 5,
; version 6), so a cascade an observation starts finishes inside that observation, the
; host drawing it a ring a frame. The deepest cascade measured on this lattice, at the
; percolation threshold near 9%, took 1,315 frames; 4,096 stands three times over it.
;
; What a rule costs (docs/SPEC.md section 2), and how this source keeps it:
;   - The lattice is numbers that count, never texts: a site in superposition is 0, an
;     observed one 10,000 plus its reading, a box 10,000,000 and an observed decay
;     10,000,000,000. A text comparison costs the language five times a number's
;     (CART.12's scoping, Found 1), and a row's sum of these codes decodes exactly into
;     its observations, its boxes and its decays.
;   - An act reaches one row of the lattice: the Probe sheet holds, for each row, the
;     column, the kind and the serial of the last act on it, and a site reads its own
;     row's three cells, so that an observation computes a row's 512 sites and never the
;     lattice's 262,144. A term every site read through $ would compute them all.
;   - The decays are computed once, from the seed, the world and the probability; the
;     readings once, from the decays; and the Field reads both, so that an act computes
;     neither.
;   - The Tally sums a row in blocks of 32 sites, so that a cascade's ring reaches a
;     block and a row's sum of its blocks, never 512 sites again.

(cartridge "superposition"
  (spec 6)                          ; the version of docs/SPEC.md this cartridge is written to: (settle K) and (bound ...) are version 6's
  (title "Superposition")           ; what the host shows
  (rate 0)                          ; an act steps the lattice; nothing else does
  (screen grid 80 50)               ; the Screen, hidden: the Camera shows the Field in its place
  (seed host)                       ; the host's seed, a new lattice each load; a seed typed into Clock!B3 brings a world back
  (settle 4096)                     ; an act's settle, at most 4,096 steps
  (bound "Field")                   ; the Field drawn to its extent and no further: the lattice is the grid
  (author "Spreadsheet Company")    ; who wrote it
  (license "0BSD")                  ; the header's twin: copy this file to start a game of your own
  (notes "Superposition: every site of the lattice is safe and decayed at once until you observe it. Space observes the site the selection stands on, B boxes it, C collapses a reading whose boxes equal it, N branches to another world. A decay observed is counted, and the experiment goes on."))

; The library whose macros this source calls: sheets, labels and headers; on, cells and
; formulas, each naming a sheet once over a run of its rows; and camera.
(include "../common.vla")

; ---- the lattice's side: this source's one parameter --------------------------------
; The lattice is n by n sites from A1 to the sheet's nth row and column, every cell of the
; Field a site and the Field bound there, n a multiple of 32, the Tally's block. Each layer
; is its first row's and first column's formulas and the rest's, so that no reference reads
; past the sheet's first row or column. A macro that hands n on, as
; Life's board-size hands its width and height on (ENGINE.9): a door that defines it again
; builds this source on another lattice, as the engine's tests build it at 64.
(defmacro (lattice-side then & args)
  "the lattice's side, 512 sites, handed on: (then 512 args...)"
  (quasiquote ((unquote then) 512 (unquote-splicing args))))

; ---- the sheets, in tab order --------------------------------------------------------
; The Field, the Observer and the Constants a person sees; the rest hidden, each a
; layer of the rule: the Decays, the Readings, the Probe, the First observation and its
; rows, the Lab's two counters, the Tally, the Screen, the Camera and the Commands.
(sheets "Field" "Observer" "Constants")
(sheet "Decays" hidden)
(sheet "Readings" hidden)
(sheet "Probe" hidden)
(sheet "First" hidden)
(sheet "FirstRow" hidden)
(sheet "Lab" hidden)
(sheet "Tally" hidden)
(sheet "Screen" hidden)
(sheet "Camera" hidden)
(sheet "Commands" hidden)

; ---- the Camera: the Field shown in the Screen's place (docs/SPEC.md section 3.8) --------
(camera 1 1)
(cells "Camera" ("A3" "sheet") ("B3" "Field"))

; ---- the commands (docs/SPEC.md section 3.10), each a key on the viewport at rate 0 ----
; Empty holds hold always. An act stands on the cell the selection stands on, and an act
; on a sheet other than the Field touches nothing (the Probe's test of Input!B19).
(headers "Commands" "A1" "name" "words" "holds" "key")
(cells "Commands"
  ("A2" "observe")  ("B2" "observe the site the selection stands on: it collapses, safe or decayed; a reading its boxes equal collapses its neighbors") ("D2" "Space")
  ("A3" "box")      ("B3" "seal the site in a box, or open the box: a box marks a site you believe has decayed") ("D3" "KeyB")
  ("A4" "collapse") ("B4" "collapse a reading whose boxes equal it: every site around it is observed") ("D4" "KeyC")
  ("A5" "branch")   ("B5" "branch to another world: a new lattice, dealt from the world's number") ("D5" "KeyN"))

; ---- the Constants: the decay probability, the assumption anyone edits ---------------
(labels "Constants" "A1" "decay probability")
(cells "Constants" ("B1" 0.15))

; ---- the Lab: the act's serial and the world ----------------------------------------
; An act is a press over a site of the Field, or a command of the three that touch it,
; standing on the Field (Input!B19); its serial counts the acts. The world counts the
; branches: every branch has its own lattice, its number in the decays' hash.
(labels "Lab" "A1" "acts" "world")
(formulas "Lab"
  ("B1" "=Lab.last!B1+IF(AND(OR(Input!$B$13=1,Input!$B$14=1,Input!$B$15=1,Input!$B$20=\"observe\",Input!$B$20=\"box\",Input!$B$20=\"collapse\"),Input!$B$19=\"Field\"),1,0)")
  ("B2" "=Lab.last!B2+IF(Input!$B$20=\"branch\",1,0)"))

; ---- the layers, each one formula over the lattice -----------------------------------
(defmacro (layers n)
  "every row whose range or whose arithmetic is the lattice's side's: the Probe, the First, the Decays, the Readings, the Field, the Tally and the Field's widths"
  (quasiquote
    (begin
      (probe (unquote n))
      (first-observation (unquote n))
      (decays (unquote n))
      (readings (unquote n))
      (field (unquote n))
      (tally (unquote n))
      (widths "Field" 1 (unquote n) 3))))

; The lattice's range, A1 to its last site; a column of it from row 1; and its three parts
; past the corner, A1: the rest of the first row, the rest of the first column, and the
; sites inside them, each of whose eight neighbors is a cell of the sheet.
(defmacro (lattice-range n)
  "A1 to the lattice's last site"
  (&expand "A1:" (address-expand n n)))
(defmacro (rows-range letters n)
  "a column's rows 1 to n"
  (&expand letters "1:" letters n))
(defmacro (top-range n)
  "the first row past the corner, B1 to the row's last site"
  (&expand "B1:" (address-expand 1 n)))
(defmacro (left-range n)
  "the first column past the corner, A2 to the column's last site"
  (&expand "A2:" (address-expand n 1)))
(defmacro (inner-range n)
  "B2 to the lattice's last site"
  (&expand "B2:" (address-expand n n)))

; The Probe: a row's last act, sticky, three cells a row: B its column, C its kind (1 an
; observation, 2 a box, 3 a collapse), D its serial. Only the row the act stands on
; changes, so that an act reaches one row of the Field.
(defmacro (probe n)
  "the Probe's three columns over the lattice's rows"
  (formulas "Probe"
    ((rows-range "B" n) "=IF(AND(OR(Input!$B$13=1,Input!$B$14=1,Input!$B$15=1,Input!$B$20=\"observe\",Input!$B$20=\"box\",Input!$B$20=\"collapse\"),Input!$B$19=\"Field\",Input!$B$12=ROW()),Input!$B$11,Probe.last!B1)")
    ((rows-range "C" n) "=IF(AND(OR(Input!$B$13=1,Input!$B$14=1,Input!$B$15=1,Input!$B$20=\"observe\",Input!$B$20=\"box\",Input!$B$20=\"collapse\"),Input!$B$19=\"Field\",Input!$B$12=ROW()),IF(OR(Input!$B$14=1,Input!$B$20=\"box\"),2,IF(OR(Input!$B$15=1,Input!$B$20=\"collapse\"),3,1)),Probe.last!C1)")
    ((rows-range "D" n) "=IF(AND(OR(Input!$B$13=1,Input!$B$14=1,Input!$B$15=1,Input!$B$20=\"observe\",Input!$B$20=\"box\",Input!$B$20=\"collapse\"),Input!$B$19=\"Field\",Input!$B$12=ROW()),Lab!$B$1,Probe.last!D1)")))

; The First observation of a world: its row and its column, 0 until it is made, and back
; to 0 at a branch. FirstRow holds, on the three rows around it, its column, and 0 on
; every other row, so that the first observation's 3 by 3 is cleared of decays by three
; rows of the Decays, 1,536 sites, and never the lattice.
(defmacro (first-observation n)
  "the First observation and its three rows"
  (labels "First" "A1" "row" "column")
  (formulas "First"
    ("B1" (&expand "=IF(Lab!$B$2<>Lab.last!$B$2,0,IF(First.last!B1>0,First.last!B1,IF(AND(OR(Input!$B$13=1,Input!$B$20=\"observe\"),Input!$B$19=\"Field\",Input!$B$12>=1,Input!$B$12<=" n ",Input!$B$11>=1,Input!$B$11<=" n "),Input!$B$12,0)))"))
    ("B2" (&expand "=IF(Lab!$B$2<>Lab.last!$B$2,0,IF(First.last!B2>0,First.last!B2,IF(AND(OR(Input!$B$13=1,Input!$B$20=\"observe\"),Input!$B$19=\"Field\",Input!$B$12>=1,Input!$B$12<=" n ",Input!$B$11>=1,Input!$B$11<=" n "),Input!$B$11,0)))")))
  (formulas "FirstRow"
    ((rows-range "B" n) "=IF(ABS(ROW()-First!$B$1)<=1,First!$B$2,0)")))

; The Decays: 1 where a site has decayed. Life's soup hash (cartridges/life) over the seed,
; the site's row and column and the world, under the probability: two linear forms reduced
; modulo the prime 67108859 and multiplied, h, and a decay where h squared, modulo the
; prime, falls under the probability's share of it. Every product stays under 2^53. The
; First observation's 3 by 3 holds no decay. The forms' constants, 3,440,100 and 3,213,021,
; are 12,345 and 54,321 with a row's and a column's multipliers added, so that each site
; keeps the world it was dealt when the lattice stood a row and a column further in, at B2.
(defmacro (decays n)
  "the Decays over the lattice"
  (formulas "Decays"
    ((lattice-range n) "=IF(AND(FirstRow!$B1>0,ABS(COLUMN()-FirstRow!$B1)<=1),0,IF(MOD(MOD(MOD(Clock!$B$3*1103515+ROW()*1597334+COLUMN()*1830421+Lab!$B$2*7919+3440100,67108859)*MOD(Clock!$B$3*2012345+ROW()*1209487+COLUMN()*1949213+Lab!$B$2*104729+3213021,67108859),67108859)*MOD(MOD(Clock!$B$3*1103515+ROW()*1597334+COLUMN()*1830421+Lab!$B$2*7919+3440100,67108859)*MOD(Clock!$B$3*2012345+ROW()*1209487+COLUMN()*1949213+Lab!$B$2*104729+3213021,67108859),67108859),67108859)<Constants!$B$1*67108859,1,0))")))

; The Readings, each site's face: a decay's code, or 10,000 plus the decays of its 3 by 3,
; the part of it on the sheet: the corner's 2 by 2, the first row's and the first column's
; 3 by 2, and the 3 by 3 inside, whose cells past the lattice's last row and column hold
; nothing.
(defmacro (reading-rule here block)
  "a site's reading, the site's decay or the decays of its block"
  (&expand "=IF(Decays!" here "=1,10000000000,10000+SUM(Decays!" block "))"))
(defmacro (readings n)
  "the Readings over the lattice, the corner's, the first row's, the first column's and the inner sites'"
  (formulas "Readings"
    ("A1" (reading-rule "A1" "A1:B2"))
    ((top-range n) (reading-rule "B1" "A1:C2"))
    ((left-range n) (reading-rule "A2" "A1:B3"))
    ((inner-range n) (reading-rule "B2" "A1:C3"))))

; The Field, every site one formula of its own last value, its eight neighbors' last
; values, its reading and its row's Probe:
;   - at a branch, every site back to superposition, 0;
;   - an act on the site this frame (its row's serial moved and its column is the site's):
;     a box toggles 0 and 10,000,000; an observation takes the reading; a collapse, or an
;     observation of a reading, turns a reading whose boxes around it equal it to 10,000
;     for one frame, so that its neighbors open as a nothing's do;
;   - else a site in superposition takes its reading when a neighbor holds 10,000, a
;     reading of nothing, so that an opening spreads a ring a frame; a box takes its reading
;     when a neighbor is a reading of nothing indeed, 10,000 on the Field and on the
;     Readings both, since nothing has decayed beside nothing, and never beside a collapse,
;     whose reading trusts its boxes; and a 10,000 takes its reading again, which is itself
;     for a nothing and the number back for a collapse.
; The rule is written once, for a site and its eight neighbors, and given four times: the
; corner's, the first row's, the first column's and the inner sites'. A neighbor off the
; sheet is the site itself, which never counts: a reading collapsing is no box, a site in
; superposition no reading of nothing, and a box no reading of nothing.
(defmacro (field-rule here row a b c d e f g h)
  "the Field's rule for the site here, its Probe's row, and its eight neighbors a to h"
  (&expand "=IF(Lab!$B$2<>Lab.last!$B$2,0,IF(AND(Probe!$D" row "<>Probe.last!$D" row ",Probe!$B" row "=COLUMN()),IF(Probe!$C" row "=2,IF(Field.last!" here "=0,10000000,IF(Field.last!" here "=10000000,0,Field.last!" here ")),IF(Field.last!" here "=0,IF(Probe!$C" row "=1,Readings!" here ",0),IF(AND(Field.last!" here ">=10001,Field.last!" here "<=10008),IF((Field.last!" a "=10000000)+(Field.last!" b "=10000000)+(Field.last!" c "=10000000)+(Field.last!" d "=10000000)+(Field.last!" e "=10000000)+(Field.last!" f "=10000000)+(Field.last!" g "=10000000)+(Field.last!" h "=10000000)=Field.last!" here "-10000,10000,Field.last!" here "),Field.last!" here "))),IF(Field.last!" here "=0,IF(OR(Field.last!" a "=10000,Field.last!" b "=10000,Field.last!" c "=10000,Field.last!" d "=10000,Field.last!" e "=10000,Field.last!" f "=10000,Field.last!" g "=10000,Field.last!" h "=10000),Readings!" here ",0),IF(Field.last!" here "=10000000,IF(OR(Field.last!" a "+Readings!" a "=20000,Field.last!" b "+Readings!" b "=20000,Field.last!" c "+Readings!" c "=20000,Field.last!" d "+Readings!" d "=20000,Field.last!" e "+Readings!" e "=20000,Field.last!" f "+Readings!" f "=20000,Field.last!" g "+Readings!" g "=20000,Field.last!" h "+Readings!" h "=20000),Readings!" here ",10000000),IF(Field.last!" here "=10000,Readings!" here ",Field.last!" here ")))))"))
(defmacro (field n)
  "the Field over the lattice: the corner's rule, the first row's, the first column's and the inner sites'"
  (formulas "Field"
    ("A1" (field-rule "A1" 1 "A1" "A1" "A1" "A1" "B1" "A1" "A2" "B2"))
    ((top-range n) (field-rule "B1" 1 "B1" "B1" "B1" "A1" "C1" "A2" "B2" "C2"))
    ((left-range n) (field-rule "A2" 2 "A2" "A1" "B1" "A2" "B2" "A2" "A3" "B3"))
    ((inner-range n) (field-rule "B2" 2 "A1" "B1" "C1" "A2" "C2" "A3" "B3" "C3"))))

; The Tally: each row of the lattice in blocks of 32 sites, a block's sum in each of the
; columns from B, then the row's sum of its blocks, and the row's sum decoded into its
; observations, its boxes and its decays; the Observer sums the decoded columns. A row's
; observed sites hold 10,000 and their readings, at most 512 and 4,096, under 10,000,000;
; its boxes 10,000,000 each, under 10,000,000,000; its decays 10,000,000,000 each.
(defmacro (tally n)
  "the Tally's blocks, its rows' sums and their decoding"
  (quasiquote
    (begin
      (tally-blocks (unquote n) 1 (unquote (quotient-expand n 32)))
      (tally-sums (unquote n) (unquote (+expand (quotient-expand n 32) 2))))))

(defmacro (tally-blocks n block blocks)
  "a column of block sums a block, from the block given to the last"
  (quote-if (>expand block blocks)
    (begin)
    (begin
      (formula "Tally" (rows-range (column-letters-expand (+expand block 1)) n)
        (&expand "=SUM(Field!" (column-letters-expand (+expand 1 (*expand 32 (-expand block 1)))) "1:" (column-letters-expand (*expand 32 block)) "1)"))
      (quasiquote (tally-blocks (unquote n) (unquote (+expand block 1)) (unquote blocks))))))

(defmacro (tally-sums n at)
  "a row's sum of its blocks in the column at, then its observations, boxes and decays in the three after"
  (formulas "Tally"
    ((rows-range (column-letters-expand at) n) (&expand "=SUM(B1:" (column-letters-expand (-expand at 1)) "1)"))
    ((rows-range (column-letters-expand (+expand at 1)) n) (&expand "=INT(MOD(" (column-letters-expand at) "1,10000000)/10000)"))
    ((rows-range (column-letters-expand (+expand at 2)) n) (&expand "=INT(MOD(" (column-letters-expand at) "1,10000000000)/10000000)"))
    ((rows-range (column-letters-expand (+expand at 3)) n) (&expand "=INT(" (column-letters-expand at) "1/10000000000)"))))

; A column row for each column from one to another, each the width given: the lattice's
; sites three characters wide, 21 pixels, so that a full screen shows about 120 by 67.
(defmacro (widths sheet from last width)
  "a column row a column, from the column given to the last"
  (quote-if (>expand from last)
    (begin)
    (begin
      (column sheet (column-letters-expand from) width shown none)
      (quasiquote (widths (unquote sheet) (unquote (+expand from 1)) (unquote last) (unquote width))))))

(lattice-side layers)

; ---- the Observer: the experiment's counts -------------------------------------------
(defmacro (observer n)
  "the Observer's counts, read from the Tally's decoded columns"
  (labels "Observer" "A1" "Superposition")
  (labels "Observer" "A3" "world" "sites observed" "boxes sealed" "decays observed" "sites in superposition" "decay probability" "seed")
  (labels "Observer" "A11" "Every site is safe and decayed at once until you observe it."
          "Space observes, B boxes, C collapses, N branches to another world." "A decay observed is counted, and the experiment goes on.")
  (formulas "Observer"
    ("B3" "=Lab!$B$2+1")
    ("B4" (&expand "=SUM(Tally!" (column-letters-expand (+expand (quotient-expand n 32) 3)) "1:" (column-letters-expand (+expand (quotient-expand n 32) 3)) n ")"))
    ("B5" (&expand "=SUM(Tally!" (column-letters-expand (+expand (quotient-expand n 32) 4)) "1:" (column-letters-expand (+expand (quotient-expand n 32) 4)) n ")"))
    ("B6" (&expand "=SUM(Tally!" (column-letters-expand (+expand (quotient-expand n 32) 5)) "1:" (column-letters-expand (+expand (quotient-expand n 32) 5)) n ")"))
    ("B7" (&expand "=" (*expand n n) "-B4-B5-B6"))
    ("B8" "=Constants!$B$1")
    ("B9" "=Clock!$B$3")))

(lattice-side observer)

; ---- the look: Lovelace Lavender ------------------------------------------------------
; A site in superposition deep lavender, #6B4FC8, and nothing drawn; an observed site pale,
; its reading's fill deepening with the count, a nothing drawing nothing; a box the logo's
; lavender with a sealed box, and an observed decay a warm red with the sign of radiation.
; Each value draws through a look (docs/SPEC.md section 7.3) whose format holds a code of
; Excel's (KERNEL.47): ;;; draws nothing, a quoted text draws itself.
(format 1 "6B4FC8" ";;;" nowrap)       ; 0, a site in superposition
(format 2 "FFFFFF" ";;;" nowrap)       ; 10,000, a reading of nothing
(format 3 "F7F4FC" "\"1\"" nowrap)     ; 10,001 to 10,008, a reading
(format 4 "EFE9FA" "\"2\"" nowrap)
(format 5 "E6DEF7" "\"3\"" nowrap)
(format 6 "DDD2F4" "\"4\"" nowrap)
(format 7 "D4C6F1" "\"5\"" nowrap)
(format 8 "CBBAEE" "\"6\"" nowrap)
(format 9 "C2AEEB" "\"7\"" nowrap)
(format 10 "B9A3E7" "\"8\"" nowrap)
(format 11 "A080E0" "\"▣\"" nowrap)    ; 10,000,000, a box
(format 12 "FFD5D5" "\"☢\"" nowrap)    ; 10,000,000,000, a decay observed
(on "Field"
  (look 0 1) (look 10000 2) (look 10001 3) (look 10002 4) (look 10003 5) (look 10004 6)
  (look 10005 7) (look 10006 8) (look 10007 9) (look 10008 10) (look 10000000 11) (look 10000000000 12)
  (gridlines on))

; The Observer's and the Constants' columns wide enough for their labels and for the seed, a number of up
; to ten digits that a person reads off to share a world (CART.12's hand test).
(on "Observer" (column "A" 24 shown none) (column "B" 14 shown none))
(on "Constants" (column "A" 20 shown none))
